# LLM call conventions

Every model call follows the same five-step shape. Do not deviate.

```ts
// app/api/questions/route.ts — the canonical pattern
import { generateObject } from 'ai';
import { models } from '@/lib/models';
import { QuestionsOutput } from '@/lib/schemas';
import { loadPrompt } from '@/lib/prompts';
import { checkQuestions } from '@/lib/guardrails';

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const input = await req.json();                       // 1. validate input with Zod first
  const system = await loadPrompt('generate-questions.v1');
  const { object } = await generateObject({             // 2. structured output, never free text
    model: models.extraction,                           // 3. cheap tier — see lib/models.ts
    system,
    prompt: buildQuestionPrompt(input),
    schema: QuestionsOutput,
  });
  const checked = checkQuestions(object, input);        // 4. deterministic guardrail
  if (!checked.ok) { /* regenerate once, else degrade */ }
  return Response.json(checked.value);                  // 5. typed response
}
```

## Rules

- `generateObject` + Zod schema for everything. Free-text generation only for the route-explanation card, and even that returns structured sections.
- Model selection via `models.extraction` / `models.reasoning` from `lib/models.ts` only.
- Prompts: `await loadPrompt('name.vN')` from `prompts/`. Bump the version when you change behaviour; keep old versions.
- Every prompt must state: the task, the exact output schema, what the model must NOT do (no protected traits, no invented facts, no ranking), and 1–2 few-shot examples from the personas in `data/personas/`.
- Log every call: model ID, token counts, latency, schema-valid yes/no. One `console.info` line via `lib/ai.ts` — this is the observability you will need on day 12.
- Timeout: 25s per call, one retry on schema-invalid, zero retries on guardrail violation (regenerate with the violation noted instead).
